clean_summary:
What if we made an LLM from scratch? Behind the scenes of mni-ml, my roommate @MankyDankyBanky and I embarked on a big project together in January 2026, inspired by @srush_nlp's minitorch curriculum. We committed to grinding through it from January to April, completing autodiff and tensor internals by February, and sharing our progress on X to stay accountable.

In March, we focused on parallelization, shipping tiled matmul using the same algorithm taught by @nvidia in their CUDA guide. By the end of March, we chose the mni-ml brand and started an educational blog. We completed minitorch ahead of schedule by March 30 and began building on top of it. April saw significant milestones, including the launch of our CUDA backend, cross-platform CI pipeline, and flash attention CUDA kernel. We recorded a demo during exam season and launched our project on April 17. We have much more in store for this summer, so stay tuned.

@mni.ml is a curriculum for understanding machine learning from scratch.
